{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Caleb silenced.</b> He silenced them all." "<b>About Moses.</b> To hear what he would say about Moses — he shouted and said: ״Did the son of Amram do only this for us?״ The listener thought he had come to speak against him, and since their hearts were already against Moses on account of the spies' words, they all fell silent to hear his disparagement. He said: ״Did he not split the sea for us, and bring down the manna for us, and provide the quail for us?״" "<b>We will surely go up.</b> Even into the heavens — and he says: Make ladders and go up there; we will succeed in all his affairs (Sotah 35)." "<b>ויהס.</b> A term of silence, as in ״הַס כָּל בָּשָׂר״ (Zechariah 2), ״הַס כִּי לֹא לְהַזְכִּיר״ (Amos 6). So is the way of people: one who wants to silence a crowd of people says שי״ט."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:46.315805015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}